{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 0, "result": {"protocolVersion": "2025-06-18", "capabilities": {"tools": {"listChanged": false}, "resources": {}, "prompts": {}}, "serverInfo": {"name": "ucas", "title": "ucas, a computer algebra system for programmers", "version": "1"}, "instructions": "ucas analyses functions (exhaustively on machine types), does exact algebra and calculus, transforms, number theory and finite fields, and finds cheaper implementations, each answer checked or proved.  Expressions are ucas syntax strings; give parameters types (x: u8, x: f32, x: real) where it matters.  Definitions persist across calls.  An ambiguous input is an error listing its readings: retry with args.assume.KEY.  structuredContent holds the typed result, checks and proof."}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 61, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "arg(1 + I) = pi/4\n  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi\n  check: equal numerically (0.7853981634, complex arithmetic)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 61, "ok": true, "cmd": "arg", "ucas": "arg 1 + I", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "arg", "input": "1 + I", "result": "pi/4"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "value", "points": 1, "max_diff": 0, "passed": true}], "files": [], "text": "arg(1 + I) = pi/4\n  the principal argument, -pi < arg <= pi\n  check: equal numerically (0.7853981634, complex arithmetic)\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 62, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the 2 square roots of 1 (w^2 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  check: each w^2, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 62, "ok": true, "cmd": "nthroots", "ucas": "nthroots 2 1", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "nthroots", "roots": [{"k": 0, "re": 1, "im": 0, "polar": "1", "exact": "1", "principal": true}, {"k": 1, "re": -1, "im": 0, "polar": "e^(i*pi)", "exact": "-1", "principal": false}], "headline": "the 2 square roots of 1 (w^2 = 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "each w^2, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically"}], "files": [], "text": "the 2 square roots of 1 (w^2 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  check: each w^2, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 63, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)\n  w2 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w3 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)\n  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 63, "ok": true, "cmd": "unity", "ucas": "unity 4", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "unity", "roots": [{"k": 0, "re": 1, "im": 0, "polar": "1", "exact": "1", "principal": true}, {"k": 1, "re": 0, "im": 1, "polar": "e^(i*pi/2)", "exact": "i", "principal": false}, {"k": 2, "re": -1, "im": 0, "polar": "e^(i*pi)", "exact": "-1", "principal": false}, {"k": 3, "re": 0, "im": -1, "polar": "e^(-i*pi/2)", "exact": "-i", "principal": false}], "headline": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically"}], "files": [], "text": "the 4 fourth roots of 1 (w^4 = 1)\n  w0 = 1                      = 1  (principal)\n  w1 = i                      = e^(i*pi/2)\n  w2 = -1                     = e^(i*pi)\n  w3 = -i                     = e^(-i*pi/2)\n  check: each w^4, parsed back as printed, equals 1 numerically\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 64, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "error (ambiguous): z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)\nambiguous: set args.assume.z to one of:\n  1) complex (default): assume.z = \"complex\"\n  2) real: annotate the variable, e.g. z: real\nrepeat the request with args.assume.z set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 64, "ok": false, "cmd": "holomorphic", "ucas": "holomorphic z^2", "structured": false, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "", "error": {"code": "ambiguous", "message": "z is taken as complex (no x or y here; say z: real for a real variable)", "key": "z", "readings": [{"index": 1, "reading": "complex", "default": true, "how": "assume.z = \"complex\""}, {"index": 2, "reading": "real", "default": false, "how": "annotate the variable, e.g. z: real"}], "how": "repeat the request with args.assume.z set to a reading (or its index), or args.defaults = true to take the default"}}, "isError": true}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 65, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "  note: x is taken as a complex variable here\npoles of 1/(x^2 + 1):\n    x = -i  order 1, residue i/2\n    x = i  order 1, residue -i/2\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re x|, |Im x| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 65, "ok": true, "cmd": "poles", "ucas": "poles 1/(x^2+1)", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "poles", "var": "x", "poles": [{"at": "-i", "order": 1, "residue": "i/2"}, {"at": "i", "order": 1, "residue": "-i/2"}]}, "notes": [{"kind": "rule", "text": "x is taken as a complex variable here"}], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "proof": {"kind": "numeric", "text": "zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid"}, "files": [], "text": "  note: x is taken as a complex variable here\npoles of 1/(x^2 + 1):\n    x = -i  order 1, residue i/2\n    x = i  order 1, residue -i/2\n  numerically: zeros of 1/f by Newton's method from a grid in |Re x|, |Im x| <= 7; orders from the growth of |f| on circles of radius 1e-2..1e-4, residues by circle integrals\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 66, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 66, "ok": true, "cmd": "multiplication_table", "ucas": "table quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "multiplication_table", "headline": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:", "details": ["|   1   i   j   k", "----+----------------", "1 |   1   i   j   k", "i |   i  -1   k  -j", "j |   j  -k  -1   i", "k |   k   j  -i  -1", "i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "multiplication table of the quaternions (row times column), not symmetric: the product does not commute:\n      |   1   i   j   k\n  ----+----------------\n    1 |   1   i   j   k\n    i |   i  -1   k  -j\n    j |   j  -k  -1   i\n    k |   k   j  -i  -1\n  i^2 = j^2 = k^2 = ijk = -1 (Hamilton); ij = k, jk = i, ki = j, and reversing a product changes its sign\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 67, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 67, "ok": true, "cmd": "algebra", "ucas": "algebra quaternion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "algebra", "commutative": "no: i j = k but j i = -k", "associative": "yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras", "alternative": "yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)", "flexible_and_power_associative": "yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra", "normed_a_composition_algebra": "yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)", "a_division_algebra": "yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras", "inverses": "every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)", "conjugation": "conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2", "headline": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "the quaternions: dimension 4 over the reals, basis 1, i, j, k\n  commutative: no: i j = k but j i = -k\n  associative: yes ((ab)c = a(bc) at 200 random triples); by Frobenius, R, C and H are the only associative real division algebras\n  alternative: yes ((aa)b = a(ab), (ba)a = b(aa) at 200 random pairs)\n  flexible and power-associative: yes ((ab)a = a(ba); powers a^n are well defined), as in every Cayley-Dickson algebra\n  normed (a composition algebra): yes, |ab| = |a||b| at 200 random pairs (Euler's four-square identity)\n  a division algebra: yes, ab = 0 only when a = 0 or b = 0 (it is normed); by Hurwitz, R, C, H and O are the only normed division algebras\n  inverses: every a != 0 has a^-1 = conj(a)/|a|^2 (a a^-1 = 1, checked)\n  conjugation: conj(ab) = conj(b) conj(a) (checked); a conj(a) = |a|^2\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 68, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 68, "ok": true, "cmd": "zerodivisors", "ucas": "zerodivisors sedenion", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "zerodivisors", "headline": "zero divisors in the sedenions:", "details": ["(e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)", "so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [], "files": [], "text": "zero divisors in the sedenions:\n  (e1 - e10)(e4 + e15) = 0, although |e1 - e10| = |e4 + e15| = sqrt(2)\n  so |ab| = |a||b| fails and the sedenions are not a division algebra (from dimension 16 on, every Cayley-Dickson algebra has them)\n"}, "isError": false}}
