{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 73, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "123456789 = 3^2 * 3607 * 3803 (not prime)\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 123456789; each factor is prime\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 73, "ok": true, "cmd": "factorint", "ucas": "factorint 123456789", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "factorint", "method": "trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)", "lhs": "123456789", "annotation": "not prime", "value": "3^2 * 3607 * 3803", "headline": "123456789 = 3^2 * 3607 * 3803 (not prime)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the product is 123456789; each factor is prime"}], "files": [], "text": "123456789 = 3^2 * 3607 * 3803 (not prime)\n  how: trial division by the primes below 50, then Pollard-Brent rho; primality by Miller-Rabin with the first 12 prime bases (deterministic below 2^64)\n  check: the product is 123456789; each factor is prime\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 74, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 74, "ok": true, "cmd": "phi", "ucas": "phi 12", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "phi", "method": "12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2", "lhs": "phi(12)", "value": "4", "value_int": 4, "headline": "phi(12) = 4", "details": ["the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent"]}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4"}], "files": [], "text": "phi(12) = 4\n  how: 12 = 2^2 * 3; phi = product of p^(e-1) (p - 1): 2^1*1 * 2\n  the order of the unit group (Z/12)*; lambda(12) = 2 is its exponent\n  check: counted the k in 1..12 with gcd(k, 12) = 1: 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 75, "result": {"content": [{"type": "text", "text": "lambda(15) = 4 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 15 = 3 * 5; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 4 (5^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(15) = 8\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 4\n"}], "structuredContent": {"id": 75, "ok": true, "cmd": "carmichael", "ucas": "carmichael 15", "structured": true, "result": {"kind": "carmichael", "method": "15 = 3 * 5; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 4 (5^1)", "lambda(2^e)": "2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(15) = 8", "headline": "lambda(15) = 4 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)"}, "notes": [], "conditions": [], "checks": [{"kind": "check", "passed": true, "text": "the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 4"}], "files": [], "text": "lambda(15) = 4 (Carmichael: the least m with a^m = 1 for every unit a)\n  how: 15 = 3 * 5; lambda is the lcm of 2 (3^1), 4 (5^1)\n  lambda(2^e) = 2^(e-2) for e >= 3; lambda(p^e) = phi(p^e) otherwise; phi(15) = 8\n  check: the lcm of the orders of all units, by stepping through their powers: 4\n"}, "isError": false}}
